WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.826
[MUSIC].

00:00:00.826 --> 00:00:05.940
There's a lot of noise in the landscape
for financial services right now.

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:11.690
We're seeing a confluence of competitive
pressures coming from different places.

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:16.000
How should companies think about
how they can either preserve,

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:21.468
strengthen or build their own competitive
modes in this changing landscape?

00:00:21.468 --> 00:00:25.760
FinTech Navigating,
it's evolving competitive and

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:31.980
regulatory landscape is really
about how FinTech's banks and

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:38.340
regulators can systematically think about
the changing competitive environment and

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:45.260
how to design and respond to
Regulations in this changing world.

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:48.570
Be it issues related to big data and
algorithms,

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:53.380
competitive strategy, digital currencies,
crypto currencies and

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:58.250
the payment system, we've brought together
a group of faculty who have thought

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:03.280
conceptually deeply about
the theoretical underpinnings and

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:07.540
roles of these different dimensions
of the financial services industry.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:11.225
And at the same time have an enormous
amount of business experience,

00:01:11.225 --> 00:01:15.559
practical experience, working with
companies to resolve specific problems.

00:01:15.559 --> 00:01:20.195
The practitioners,
the participants in these programs, and

00:01:20.195 --> 00:01:26.418
the faculty spend an enormously fruitful
week, understanding how to prioritize.

00:01:26.418 --> 00:01:29.633
Understanding how to cut
through the noise, and

00:01:29.633 --> 00:01:34.653
see what the clear underlying fundamental
issues are, and to begin to frame

00:01:34.653 --> 00:01:39.832
solutions to the problems that they're
facing within their own businesses or

00:01:39.832 --> 00:01:45.023
in their own challenge in designing
regulation to move the industry forward.

00:01:45.023 --> 00:01:49.862
We're going to be drawing broadly upon the
strength of Stanford in terms of its human

00:01:49.862 --> 00:01:51.701
capital, but also our style and

00:01:51.701 --> 00:01:55.080
location here in terms of
the entrepreneurial spirit.

00:01:55.080 --> 00:02:00.370
This diversity of perspectives and human
capital, will all be in the room together,

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:04.870
challenging each other,
appreciating each other's challenges.

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:10.430
Working together to begin to
see how to develop frameworks

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:15.260
that they can take back and share more
broadly within their own companies.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:20.180
There's such an opportunity
right now to bring

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:25.740
greater clarity to these cross currents of

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:30.330
economic pressures and
changing regulations.

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:34.340
And who are going to be the winners,
who are going to be the losers,

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:39.920
this is a perfect environment to take up
these issues, to challenge ourselves.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:43.477
And there's just a fantastic group
of faculty stirring it all up.

00:02:43.477 --> 00:02:46.532
[MUSIC]

